prompt:
The library function `arr::reverse_ends` has no postcondition. Give it one stating that the first and last elements are exchanged and every other element is unchanged, keeping its parameters, precondition and body.

Required signature (in unit `arr`):
fn reverse_ends(a: &mut [i64]) -> ()

reference.code:
spec fn ends_swapped(a: &[i64], b: &[i64]) -> bool { a.len() > 0 && swapped(a, b, 0, a.len() - 1) }

#[effects(pure)]
#[uses(idx2, nonempty, swapped, ends_swapped)]
fn reverse_ends(a: &mut [i64]) -> ()
    requires nonempty(a),
    ensures ends_swapped(a, old(a)),
{
    let n: usize = a.len();
    swap(a, 0, n - 1);
}
